cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Zhen: fast, complete host discovery for macOS local networks"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Juan Carlos"
    family-names: "Estévez Rodríguez"
    alias: JCTec
repository-code: "https://github.com/JCTec/zhen"
abstract: >-
  A native macOS network scanner written entirely in Swift 6, with no
  subprocesses and no external binaries. Host discovery runs unprivileged over
  ICMP datagram sockets; retransmission timing adapts per host and is decoupled
  from the budget used to declare a host absent, which is what makes the sweep
  fast without trading away completeness. Device names come from fusing mDNS,
  SSDP and NetBIOS rather than from OS fingerprinting, and identity survives
  randomised hardware addresses.
keywords:
  - network scanning
  - host discovery
  - Swift
  - macOS
  - mDNS
  - adaptive timing
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
